# Elixir pipe operator

## Transform nested code into a pipeline

The Elixir pipe operator (`|>`) is a core language feature that takes the result of the expression on its left-hand side and automatically injects it as the first argument into the function call on its right-hand side.

```elixir
# Difficult to read; evaluates from the inside out.
String.replace(String.downcase(String.trim("  Hello World  ")), "hello", "hi")
```

Versus:

```elixir
"  Hello World  "
|> String.downcase()
|> String.trim()
|> String.replace("hello", "hi")
```
